\title{DISCO computation and modality decomposition}
\description{
Computation of the Distance of Covariance (DISCO), a correlation-based measure of homeostatic dysregulation. DISCO quantifies, for each individual, how much the pairwise correlation structure of a set of biomarkers deviates from that of a young reference population, weighted by the age-association of each biomarker. The package provides the core 'cal_disco()' function (with single-threaded, parallel and Rcpp/OpenMP backends) and a block-wise decomposition helper. See Hao et al. "Distance of Covariance (DISCO): A Novel Measure of Network Homeostatic Dysregulation Reveals Organ System Interconnections Underlying Mortality and Disease Risk".
